ON THE FIGURES THIS SOFTWARE PRODUCES

This is measurement software for irrigated agriculture. Anyone redistributing
it, or publishing figures from it, should carry the following forward, because
these are not disclaimers of convenience - they are the conditions under which
the outputs mean anything at all.

  Equity figures describe measured differences in outcome along a canal. A
  head-to-tail gap has many possible causes - siltation, upstream abstraction,
  soil, crop choice, planting date - and this software separates none of them.
  No figure it produces attributes anything to any office, operator or decision,
  and none should be presented as if it did.

  Radar shows standing water, not flow. A canal full and static reads
  identically to one carrying its design discharge.

  Rangeland and corridor outputs describe vegetation and surface water only.
  They say nothing about who may use land, and are not evidence of any claim by
  any party. In contexts where farmer-herder tension is live, presenting them as
  such would cause harm this software is explicitly designed to avoid.

  Absolute nitrogen and yield figures are withheld unless a locally calibrated
  model exists and clears a stated error limit. Removing those gates would
  produce confident numbers that nobody can defend.

  Sample geometry and sample results distributed with this software are
  synthetic and are labelled as such in the files themselves. They demonstrate
  the shape of the output and are not measurements of any real canal, field or
  rangeland.

THIRD-PARTY DATA

This software reads public Earth observation datasets through Google Earth
Engine, including Copernicus Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 (ESA), Landsat 8/9
(USGS/NASA), CHIRPS (UCSB/USGS), ERA5-Land (ECMWF/Copernicus), MODIS and
GRACE-FO (NASA), JRC Global Surface Water (European Commission), and NOAA GFS.
Each carries its own terms and citation requirements, which are not granted or
altered by the Apache License covering this software.
